{"user": "what did I do wrong?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:05:43.851363+00:00", "assistant": "Nothing \u201crules-wrong\u201d \u2014 but strategically, the big issue was **corner control**.\n\nFinal score looks like:\n\n- **White: 41**\n- **Black: 23**\n\nWhite won by **18**.\n\nWhat hurt most:\n\n1. **White got 3 corners**: **a1, h1, a8**.  \n   Corners cannot be flipped back, so they anchor lots of stable edge discs.\n\n2. **Black had many middle discs**, but middle discs are easy to flip late.\n\n3. In the endgame, you likely focused on **flipping more discs immediately**, but the better idea is often:  \n   **force White into bad moves, take corners, and count the final result.**\n\nMain lesson: near the end, don\u2019t ask \u201cwhich move flips most?\u201d Ask:  \n**\u201cAfter I move, what corner or edge does White get?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:05:50.431447+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:05:53.287397+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1, "Paraphrase": 1, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Paraphrase": 0.3333333333333333, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint"